Z||000005||Fformula88||12-10-2001||01:02 PM||||I guess it really depends on your definition of "cool cars".  It loks like things that are different, like the AWD Celica or fairly rare cars.<P>How about the Mazda RX-8... it will be out soon.  Its a 4 door coupe (suicide rear doors) but is bringing back the Rotary engine!  Very cool IMO.<P>Add the new Nissan 350-Z to my list.  Its going to have well over 250 HP out of a V6 and start under $30K.  Also very cool IMO.<P>Subaru's WRX with 227 HP turbo 4 and AWD is a cool setup, although I am not crazy about the styling (or 4 doors).<P>Also, pocket rockets maybe be better than they ever were performance-wise... and certainly with their abundance.  Focus SVT, Sentra SE-R, Civic Si.  Both the RSX-Type S and the Celica GTS have amazing power outputs from small displacement fours, and especially the GTS offer outstanding handling.<P>Throw the number of roadsters and sports cars available, MR2 Spyder, Miata, S2000, Z3 etc etc with some being very affordable, and I think there are a lot of cool cars still available.||||reg||1
