Z||000025||Formula88||12-11-2001||09:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>How about these?<P>The Super Duty Grand Am (1973)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good list, but there never was a Super Duty Grand Am.  Yes, it was Motor Trend's Car of the Year in 73, but that was a pre-production model.  The Super Duty engine project was cut back and they didn't have enough engines for both the T/A and the G/A, so the T/A got them all.<P>How about '69 Trans Am Convertibles?  Only 8 made!  7 of the 8 have been accounted for, 1 is still missing.<P>72 Trans Am - Only ~1200 made.  Next rarest year (697 made in '69).  Last year for the 455HO (the real HO, not the re-badged station wagon engine used in '75-76)<P>How about an old ~'60 Tempest with a front mounted engine and a rear mounted transaxle with the "rope" driveshaft!  The drive shaft was a flexible material without U-joints at either end, and would bow in the middle - hence the "rope" nickname.<P>Pontiac 6000 Diesel - rare? yes.  Valuable, that's debatable. <P>'80-81 Turbo Trans Am.  The first, and to date only, production turbo V8 produced in America.<P><BR>||||reg||1
